# ============================================================================
#  SwitchTester — .gitattributes
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
#  Line-ending policy. Without this file the behaviour depends on each machine's
#  core.autocrlf — set to `true` by the Git for Windows installer, in the SYSTEM
#  config — which is why "LF will be replaced by CRLF" warnings appear and why
#  tool-edited files drift into mixed endings.
#
#  Policy: LF in the repository AND in the working tree.
#
#  LF is chosen over the Windows CRLF convention for a practical reason, not an
#  aesthetic one. Four things write these files: git checkout, the CubeIDE
#  editor, agent tooling, and CubeMX codegen. Only CubeMX cannot be told to emit
#  LF — and its output is bounded to Core/ and normalised on commit anyway.
#  Agent tooling cannot be told to emit CRLF at all, and it edits everywhere.
#
#  Companion settings — neither is carried by this file:
#    - core.autocrlf=false, set LOCALLY. Never --global: other repos on this
#      machine rely on the system value.
#    - CubeIDE: Project > Properties > Resource > New text file line delimiter
#      = Unix. Project-scoped — NOT the workspace preference of the same name,
#      which would reach every project in the workspace. Eclipse PRESERVES an
#      existing file's delimiter and only imposes one on files it creates, so
#      once the tree is LF, hand edits keep it LF indefinitely.
#
#  Audit:  git ls-files --eol | awk '{print $2}' | sort | uniq -c
#          A clean tree reads w/lf throughout, except w/-text binaries.
# ============================================================================

# Default: detect text vs binary, normalise text to LF in the repo and on disk.
*               text=auto eol=lf

# --- Sources and build inputs (stated rather than left to detection) ---
*.c             text
*.h             text
*.s             text
*.ld            text

# --- Docs, data, host-side scripts ---
*.md            text
*.txt           text
*.json          text
*.py            text
*.ps1           text

# --- CubeIDE / CubeMX project files ---
# Tracked deliberately (see .gitignore) and kept text so diffs stay readable.
*.ioc           text
*.project       text
*.cproject      text
*.mxproject     text
*.launch        text

# --- Must be CRLF wherever they land ---
# cmd.exe can mis-parse labels and goto in an LF-only batch file.
*.bat           text eol=crlf
*.cmd           text eol=crlf

# --- Never converted, never diffed as text ---
*.pdf           binary
*.bin           binary
*.elf           binary
*.hex           binary
*.a             binary
